🚀 Level-1: Basic String Patterns
1️⃣ Traversal Pattern (Character by Character)
👉 Learn how to loop through characters in a string.
Examples:
    Count vowels
    Count uppercase/lowercase
    Count digits

2️⃣ Reverse String Pattern
👉 Learn different ways to reverse a string.
Examples:
    Reverse entire string
    Reverse words in a sentence
    Reverse characters of each word

3️⃣ Palindrome Pattern
👉 Check if a string reads the same forward & backward.
Examples:
    Check palindrome string
    Longest palindrome substring (advanced)
4️⃣ Frequency / Counting Pattern
    👉 Count how many times a character appears.
Examples:
    Character frequency
    Most frequent character
    First unique character
************************************************************

🚀 Level-2: Two-Pointer String Patterns
5️⃣ Two-Pointer Pattern
👉 For problems like palindrome, reverse, trimming spaces.
Examples:
    Remove extra spaces
    Reverse using two pointers
    Check if two strings are anagrams (after sort)
6️⃣ Sliding Window (String Version)
👉 Very powerful for substring problems.
Examples:
    Longest substring without repeating characters
    Longest substring with K distinct characters
    Minimum window substring

🚀 Level-3: Substring / Subsequence Patterns
7️⃣ All Substrings Pattern (Brute Force)
👉 Generate every substring for analysis.
Common Problems:
    Count palindromic substrings
    Find substring with specific sum or pattern
8️⃣ Subsequence Pattern (Recursive / Bitmask)
👉 Used for combinations and string subsets.
Examples:
    Generate all subsequences
    Find the longest common subsequence
🚀 Level-4: String Transformation Patterns
9️⃣ String Builder / Mutable String Pattern
👉 Efficient modifications using StringBuilder.
Examples:
    Remove characters
    Insert/remove characters efficiently
    Replace characters
🔟 Tokenizing / Splitting Pattern
    👉 Work with words instead of characters.
Examples:
    Count words
    Reverse words
    Split by special characters
1️⃣1️⃣ Sorting Characters Pattern
👉 Sorting helps solve many problems.
Examples:
Are two strings anagrams?
Sort letters alphabetically
🚀 Level-5 Advanced Patterns
1️⃣2️⃣ HashMap + String Pattern
👉 Used in anagram problems and frequency maps.
Examples:
    Group Anagrams
    Check isomorphic strings
    First non-repeating character
1️⃣3️⃣ Regex / Pattern-Matching Pattern
👉 Very powerful for filtering/validating strings.
Examples:
    Validate email
    Validate mobile number
    Extract digits/words
1️⃣4️⃣ DP (Dynamic Programming) String Pattern
👉 Hard but useful for interviews.
Examples:
    Longest Palindromic Subsequence
    Edit Distance
    Word Break Problem

🏆 Summary of All String Patterns
| Level | Pattern        | Use                         |
| ----- | -------------- | --------------------------- |
| 1     | Traversal      | Basic character operations  |
| 1     | Reverse        | String manipulation         |
| 1     | Palindrome     | Checks, two-pointer intro   |
| 1     | Frequency      | HashMap skills              |
| 2     | Two-Pointer    | Efficient scanning          |
| 2     | Sliding Window | Optimal substring problems  |
| 3     | Substring      | Pattern search, brute force |
| 3     | Subsequence    | Recursive patterns          |
| 4     | StringBuilder  | Efficient editing           |
| 4     | Splitting      | Word-level operations       |
| 4     | Sorting        | Anagram problems            |
| 5     | HashMap        | Complex patterns            |
| 5     | Regex          | Validation                  |
| 5     | DP             | Hard interview problems     |

